From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:59:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 159/181] fix(polecat): stop claiming the WORK bead and re-key
 the live-owner guard to the molecule's last holder (gcp-952j9)

The fork's polecat claimed its WORK bead in_progress for the whole run
(gcp-5gir's claim, hardened by gcp-cvbs's work-bead claim guard). That claim
forced two interim workarounds in the restack: de377194's re-pointed-step close
(a gc.step_ref fallback when `gc hook current` is not this session's
submit-and-exit step) and a0c62491's --if-assignee takeover (bd >= 1.3 refuses
to reassign another actor's in_progress bead), plus the STEP_REPOINTED block in
the startup claim. The claim was also the only reason `gc hook --claim` ever
handed the WORK bead back, through its crash-recovery tier.

Upstream never claims WORK and only the refinery handoff writes it. That is
safe: the pool's tier-3 query serves only beads carrying gc.routed_to=<pool>
with no assignee, the graph.v2 sling never stamps gc.routed_to on WORK, and
`gc sling` refuses a second pour onto a live workflow. So this commit retires
the claim and everything it forced:

- workspace-setup step 1 loses the claim span (CLAIM_GUARD work-bead block and
  prose). The base-resolve edit from gcp-19hoi stays byte-for-byte.
- submit-and-exit's twelve drain sites return to #490's three-line form
  (`gc hook current --id-only` || exit 1, then the in-progress submit-and-exit
  check). This is `git revert` of de377194, minus its dead STEP_SESSION.
  HANDOFF_FAILED stays: it still guards a genuinely refused write.
- the polecat prompt drops the --if-assignee takeover arm and STEP_REPOINTED.
- the live-owner guard no longer reads the WORK bead's assignee, which nothing
  sets now. It keys on the molecule's last holder: the claimed step's own
  polecat_session (a release touches only status and assignee), else the most
  recently updated sibling step that names an assignee. qjkp's decision block
  is unchanged, so a live crew seat as last holder still proceeds; the restore
  takes gc.session_id from the live row.

Tests: test_polecat_work_bead_claim_guard.sh and its allowlist row go.
test_polecat_live_owner_guard.sh seeds the last holder from a sibling step
(17 cases: three takeover cases out, test_duplicate_pour_declines_with_the_
work_bead_unclaimed, test_released_step_names_its_own_last_holder and
test_crew_assignee_on_the_work_bead_is_never_read in).
test_work_bead_is_claimed_for_the_whole_run becomes
test_work_bead_is_never_claimed. The drain-ack test keeps the 12 "hook names the
step" cases and gains 24 that refuse when the hook names the WORK bead or
cannot answer. test_polecat_artifact_dir.sh loses its claim-call scaffolding.

Follow-up: the resume re-verify still keys on the WORK assignee (gcp-o1nij).
Pin transition: move the city pin past this merge only when no in-progress
WORK bead still carries a polecat_session equal to its assignee.

Fold at the next baseline upgrade: drop the retired patches and fix up this commit's remaining hunks into their introducing patches; the replayed tree must equal the pre-fold tree (gcp-k6301).

